OpenWings patch 0009: run the agent's python and bash in the code runner

Upstream runs agent code only inside bubblewrap containment
(src/containment.py). The upstream image does not ship bubblewrap and
Docker's default seccomp profile blocks the namespaces it needs, so in a
Docker deployment python and bash always refuse ("containment
unavailable"). With the runner compose profile on, OpenWings sends the code,
after upstream's own checks (no sudo, no ad-hoc HTTP downloads, resource
identity), to the runner container: no network, no secrets, read-only root,
all capabilities dropped, CPU/memory/process caps, and only the agent
workspace writable (wings/runner.py, docker/runner/).

  * src/agent_tools/subprocess_tools.py: _run_owned_command, the single
    choke point both tools use, delegates to wings.runner.run_owned() when
    the runner is enabled. Without it, upstream behaviour is unchanged.
  * src/tool_schemas.py: python and bash describe the runner, its
    libraries, and that saved images appear in the chat.
  * src/agent_runtime/authority.py, src/tool_execution.py: fixes an
    upstream bug that made every exact-approved process launch fail
    ("Producer operation has no request admission or exact claim"): around
    each tool call tool_execution rebinds the running request's own
    authority, restricted by the tool policy, and intersect() marks every
    result inherited (a child), which exact approvals refuse. Only that
    rebinding, and only when the authority is a pure restriction of the
    active one, now keeps the active authority's flag. intersect() itself is
    unchanged, so child runs and any authority with other grants or
    resources stay inherited (upstream's child approval tests pass).
    Unreachable upstream in Docker until code could run at all.
  * app.py, static/js/wings-ui.js: "Workspace files" page and sidebar entry
    to download what the agent wrote (wings/files_routes.py, admins only).

OpenWings also sets ODYSSEUS_WORKSPACE_DEFAULT=/workspaces/default (compose), an
upstream setting the web UI already honours: without a bound workspace,
upstream refuses every file and code tool in an ordinary chat.

